  "_about": "Ronda 20b, palanca 6. commandSearch: the names a window's search of its own orders is drawn with (a command palette, a «tell me» box); only an order is looked up there. lookingGoals: the first words of a goal that only checks what is on screen (never an order for that search). viewOptionLabels: the label a window writes beside the control that shows the current option of its view or its order; viewOptionLabels.view/.sort/.group split it by the family of the option the goal names (review 3, finding 2). frameNavigation: the window's frame and its navigation buttons, never a search's result (back, up, refresh, the address band). assistantCommand (ronda 24, v3-07): the first words of a command that calls an assistant; the blind unfolding before a «none» never opens one.",
